 line of strong\nthunderstorms extending from near Commerce City to over western\nParker, or extending from 8 miles northeast of Denver to 17 miles\nsoutheast of Denver, moving northeast at 15 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nEastern Denver, Aurora, eastern Centennial, eastern Commerce City,\nParker, Denver International Airport, D.I.A Terminal and\nConcourses, Buckley SFB, Arapahoe Park and Foxfield.","ends":"2026-09-18T17:15:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"North Douglas County Below 6000 Feet/Denver/West Adams and Arapahoe Counties/East Broomfield County; Elbert/Central and East Douglas Counties Above 6000 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c9870f01e2eec2a6ace2712fbb9bd208fd82d687.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c9870f01e2eec2a6ace2712fbb9bd208fd82d687.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-09-18T20:10:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 182010 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 210 PM MDT Fri Sep 18 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Increasing coverage and intensity of afternoon/evening showers and t-storms for the lower elevations, peaking Saturday when locally heavy rainfall can be expected across the plains. - Warm temperatures through Saturday to give way to more seasonal conditio","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-09-18T20:04:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Wednesday...Scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms are expected through early to mid evening, bringing isolated heavy rain and elevated humidity levels. Winds will remain light outside of brief gusty outflow from any convection. Numerous showers and thunderstorms are expected Saturday with widespread coverage over the plains